* {{i|Monstro's Lung|na}}: Same effect as {{i|20/20}}, except retains fire rate.
* {{i|Mom's Eye}}: Grants a chance to shoot an extra bomb from the back of Isaac's head.
** '''Mom's Eye''' + {{I|Eye of the Occult}}: Bombs that spawn from Mom's Eye will try to move to where you're shooting making it very difficult to not get hit by your own explosions.
* {{i|Mom's Knife|nar}}: Overrides Dr. Fetus.
* {{i|My Reflection}}: The bombs lose momentum and slide back towards Isaac, making self-damage very likely.
* {{T|Ouroboros Worm}}: Does not affect the trajectory of the bombs. Turns some bombs into homing bombs, similar to {{I|Bobby-Bomb}}.
* {{I|Parasitoid|r}}: Bomb explosions have a chance of leaving the slowing creep in a larger pool than egg sack tears, {{dlc|nr+}} however the egg sack bombs can't spawn [[Blue fly|Blue Flies]]/[[Blue spider|Blue Spiders]].
* {{dlc|nr}} [[Tear Effects|Piercing tears]]: The bombs pierce through enemies, which makes killing them more difficult.
* {{I|Soy Milk|na}}: Rapidly shoots very low damage bombs. Can create a line of bombs which can knock each other back, which can be difficult to avoid taking damage from.
** {{dlc|anr}} Rapidly shoots medium damage bombs. Can create a line of bombs which can knock each other back, which can be difficult to avoid taking damage from.
** {{dlc|r}} Rapidly shoots low damage mini-bombs. Bombs don't knock each other back.
* [[Spectral tears]]: The bombs can pierce through the obstacles. If a bomb is fired inside an obstacle, the bomb collides against it, but not against others.
* {{I|Spirit Sword}}: Overrides Dr. Fetus.
** '''Spirit Sword''' + {{I|Haemolacria|n}}: The split bombs can appear from Spirit Sword's projectiles.
* {{i|Sticky Bombs}}: The bombs stick to enemies ({{dlc|nr}} unless Isaac has piercing), but enemies killed by the bomb will not spawn Blue Spiders.
** {{dlc|r}} The bombs always spawn slowing white creep after exploding.
* {{i|Tear Detonator}}: No effect on bombs.
* {{dlc+|r}} [[Tear height]] ups such as {{t|Tape Worm}}, {{i|Jupiter}}, {{i|Telepathy For Dummies}}, {{p|I - The Magician}}, and {{p|Huge Growth}}: Improves the effective range of the bombs.{{dlc-}}
* {{i|Technology 2|r}}: The bombs are pushed forward by the laser.
* {{i|Technology Zero}}: Dr. Fetus bombs do not generate electricity. Tears from other sources such as {{I|Sad Bombs}} can still generate electricity.
* {{I|The Wiz}}: Causes Isaac to fire two bombs instead of one in diagonal directions.
* {{i|Tiny Planet}}: The bombs fly uncontrollably around the player, making self-damage very likely.
* {{i|Tractor Beam}}: After firing a bomb and moving, the bomb will have a homing-style effect towards the beam, but will not stay directly on the beam. '''Not recommended''', as changing directions while firing will cause the bomb to reel back to Isaac at high speed, making self-damage very likely.

